dcomp: keep the composition thread running while a target's window exists

The compositor thread of dcomp-steinberg ends as soon as one tick drew
nothing (no target ticked successfully, or a target had no root) and is only
started again by IDCompositionDevice::Commit(). A program that does not
commit again has nothing drawn from then on: Cubase 14's window stayed as it
was after a minimize and restore, because the restore commits nothing.

Count a target for as long as its window exists, whatever the tick returned,
so the thread ends only when every window of the device is gone (and Commit()
starts it again). Skip drawing while the target's top level window is
minimized: the first tick after the restore redraws every visual, and the
window's surface was not worth keeping up meanwhile. Skipping windows that
no longer exist also stops the thread drawing on a destroyed hwnd.

Layers on dcomp-swapchain-present-offscreen. Untested in Cubase; built only.

--- a/dlls/dcomp/device.c
+++ b/dlls/dcomp/device.c
@@ -898,20 +898,32 @@
         count = 0;
         LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY(target, &device->targets, struct composition_target, entry)
         {
+            /* Skip targets created from a shared visual handle. Composition for such targets will
+             * be done for the visual tree where the visual created from the shared visual handle is at */
+            if (target->shared_visual_handle)
+                continue;
+
+            /* The thread is only restarted by Commit(), which a program that has nothing new
+             * to say never calls: a tick that failed once, a target without a root yet or a
+             * minimized window used to end it for good, and the window stayed as it was when
+             * it came back.  A target counts while its window exists. */
+            if (!IsWindow(target->hwnd))
+                continue;
+            count++;
+
             if (!target->root)
             {
                 FIXME("Target %p has no root.\n", &target->IDCompositionTarget_iface);
                 continue;
             }
 
-            /* Skip targets created from a shared visual handle. Composition for such targets will
-             * be done for the visual tree where the visual created from the shared visual handle is at */
-            if (target->shared_visual_handle)
+            /* Nothing to show, and the window's surface is not the program's to keep up
+             * while it is minimized; the first tick after the restore draws it all. */
+            if (IsIconic(GetAncestor(target->hwnd, GA_ROOT)))
                 continue;
 
             visual = impl_from_IDCompositionVisual(target->root);
-            if (SUCCEEDED(composite_target_tick(target, visual)))
-                count++;
+            composite_target_tick(target, visual);
         }
 
         if (!count)
